  "definition_id": "bd39dd92-4375-5c58-ae5c-d99bfc4e0015",
  "source": "package",
  "name": "Siril rl",
  "description": "Restores an image using the Richardson-Lucy method.\n\nOptionally, a PSF may be loaded using the argument -loadpsf=filename (created with MAKEPSF).\n\nThe number of iterations is provide by -iters (the default is 10).\n\nThe type of regularization can be set with -tv for Total Variation, or -fh for the Frobenius norm of the Hessian matrix (the default is none) and -alpha= provides the regularization strength (lower value = more regularization, default = 3000).\n\nBy default the gradient descent method is used with a default step size of 0.0005, however the multiplicative method may be specified with -mul .\n\nThe stopping criterion may be activated by specifying a stopping limit with -stop=\n\nLinks: psf , makepsf\n\nUses fixed input references and writes only invocation-owned outputs. Optional argument values are sent only when their use_* control is true; zero is preserved.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "name": "image",
      "type": "APF_SCIENCE"
    },
    {
      "name": "psf",
      "type": "APF_SCIENCE"
    }
  ],
  "outputs": [
    {
      "name": "image",
      "type": "APF_SCIENCE"
    }
  ],
